Invariants and cautions

• Similar visible colors can have different optical spectra (metamerism), and perception depends on illuminant and observer.
• The sound mapping is a mathematical choice; visible wavelengths do not prescribe guitar notes, nor does life select seven rainbow notes.
• A creative translation must never masquerade as an authentic traditional symbol; retain stewardship and rights.
• Mathematical equivalence, causal mechanism, functional analogy and artistic metaphor must be labeled separately.
• Interpretable empty space and missing notes require established expectations.
• Store original sources separately from invented continuations. Prestige only validated operators and prune errors.

